1. PROJECT MISSION — DO NOT CHANGE THE CORE IDEA

SPHEREx ATLAS is a public-facing astronomical exploration platform designed to help users explore SPHEREx observations of the sky over time.

SPHEREx surveys the entire sky in 102 near-infrared spectral bands, allowing scientists to investigate astronomical objects and their properties.

The core experience must allow users to:

1. Enter celestial coordinates (Right Ascension and Declination).
2. Search the real SPHEREx archive for observations of that sky region.
3. Discover available observations and their actual observation dates.
4. Retrieve real astronomical image products when accessible.
5. Display observations chronologically.
6. Explore image changes over time.
7. Compare compatible observations.
8. Explore spectral information when actual suitable data is available.
9. Inspect FITS image metadata, WCS information, and scientific measurements.
10. Distinguish real scientific data from external, simulated, unavailable, and unverified data.

The application must remain honest about the limitations of the actual SPHEREx archive.

Never fabricate observations, dates, scientific measurements, spectra, detections, or archive provenance.

